WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.400
Module 4 asked questions such as how many how much
or what

00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:08.275
is the average Module 5 asks a different question
which rule applies

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.950
A decision rule can involve several conditions at
once For example a

00:00:13.975 --> 00:00:17.912
record might qualify only when it is active consent
is explicitly true

00:00:18.138 --> 00:00:22.050
a diagnosis belongs to a target set and usable
contact information is

00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:26.875
missing Some of those fields may be NULL That is why
this

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:32.712
module emphasizes structure Define the condition
inspect missingness group related tests

00:00:32.725 --> 00:00:36.938
with parentheses order CASE branches carefully and
test boundary values such as

00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:41.675
zero blank text FALSE and NULL The goal is not
merely SQL

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.125
that runs The goal is SQL whose output matches the
written rule
